From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cix: amvx: default the decoder capture port to NV12

mvx_v4l2_fops.c sets BOTH ports to V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_AFBC_8 on open. For a
decoder the capture port is the raw output side, so any client that probes the
device before configuring it is handed Arm's proprietary AFBC format - and
clients that cannot name AFBC give up there rather than enumerating further.

GStreamer's V4L2 decoders were dead on this hardware for exactly that reason:

    gst-launch-1.0 ... ! v4l2h264dec ! fakesink
    ERROR: Video device uses an unsupported pixel format.

despite v4l2h264dec advertising video/x-raw(memory:DMABuf) with drm-format
NV12/YU12/P010 - it is willing to take dmabufs from this decoder, it just never
reaches negotiation. The same default is what breaks stock Chromium's V4L2 path.

With the decoder capture default changed to NV12, measured on Sky1:

  - gst-launch v4l2h264dec / v4l2h265dec / v4l2av1dec all decode clean, where
    all three previously failed at probe.
  - Epiphany (WebKitGTK 2.52.5, which routes media through GStreamer) hardware
    decodes H.264 1080p, HEVC 1080p and 4K, and AV1 1080p and 4K, with
    WebKitWebProcess holding /dev/video0 during playback.
  - Chromium NCZ Sky1 is unaffected: re-ran the full matrix, still 10/10
    hardware across five codecs at 1080p and 4K.

Scope is deliberately narrow. Only the decoder's capture default moves; the
coded-side default is untouched because decoder clients always set it
explicitly, and the encoder is left alone since its raw side is the OUTPUT port
- a different case that was not tested here. AFBC remains fully available as an
explicit choice; it is simply no longer what an unconfigured device advertises.

Upstream-Status: Pending (to be sent to CIX)
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/driver/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_fops.c
+++ b/driver/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_fops.c
@@ -85,6 +85,17 @@
     (void)mvx_v4l2_vidioc_s_fmt_vid_out(file, NULL, &fmt);
 
     fmt.type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE;
+    if (!ctx->is_encoder) {
+        /*
+         * A decoder's capture port is the raw output side. Default it to NV12,
+         * not AFBC, so that clients which probe the device before configuring
+         * it see a format they can name. GStreamer's v4l2 decoders abort with
+         * "Video device uses an unsupported pixel format" when handed AFBC at
+         * probe time, and the same default breaks stock Chromium's V4L2 path.
+         * AFBC is unaffected as an explicit choice.
+         */
+        fmt.fmt.pix.pixelformat = V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12;
+    }
     (void)mvx_v4l2_vidioc_s_fmt_vid_cap(file, NULL, &fmt);
 
     if (!ctx->is_jpeg) {
